@startuml 4-4-line-processing
' 4-4. A message (text / image) arrives while the session is PROCESSING - the worker is answering the previous round
' Traced from code at dev-rewrite e09d47b (2026-10-11) . box = file . arrow = function calls function
' italic = what that function does to PSQL / Redis
' PROCESSING = session:{id}:state is PROCESSING (set by session.start_processing in run_chat)
' The outcome depends on whether the message arrives before or after the worker calls session.read_buffer
' Cases A and B were run against the real code on the test database (2026-10-11):
'   case B: the second message stayed pending, and the AI did not see it in that round or the next one
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox
autonumber

title 4-4. Message arrives while the session is PROCESSING

actor "LINE\n(reporter)" as LINE
participant "controllers/\nline.py" as CTRL
participant "services/\nsession.py" as SESS
participant "workers/\nworker.py" as WORKER
participant "clients/\ndatabase.py\n(PSQL)" as CDB
participant "clients/\nredis.py\n(Redis)" as CRD

note over WORKER : run_chat has passed session.start_processing\nstate = PROCESSING

== the new message hits the webhook (same in both cases) ==
LINE -> CTRL : POST /webhook/line -> ... -> on_message(event)
ref over CTRL, CRD
  same as 4-1 from user.find_by_line_id through session.buffer(message)
  the message is saved to PSQL (pending), appended to the buffer, last_message_at = now
end ref
CTRL -> SESS : session.start_buffering(current)
SESS -> CRD : set_buffering_if_idle(session_id)\n<i>SET session:{id}:state BUFFERING NX</i>
CRD --> SESS : False
SESS --> CTRL : False
note right of CTRL
  the key already exists (PROCESSING) -> set fails
  job.enqueue_chat is not called
end note
CTRL --> LINE : 200 "OK"

== case A - it arrives before the worker calls session.read_buffer ==
note over WORKER : during user.line_id_for, line.show_loading
WORKER -> SESS : session.read_buffer(session_id)
SESS -> CRD : get_buffer(session_id)
CRD --> SESS : list[Message] - includes the new message
SESS --> WORKER : list[Message]
ref over WORKER, CRD
  same as 4-2 onward through session.finish
  the new message goes with this round, line.reply uses its reply_token
end ref

== case B - it arrives after the worker has called session.read_buffer ==
note over WORKER
  during image download, the AI call, line.reply
  the buffer the worker holds does not contain the new message
end note
WORKER -> SESS : session.finish(session_id, buffer, new_context, answer)
SESS -> CDB : insert_bot_message(session_id, answer)
SESS -> CDB : mark_answered([message_id of the messages the worker read])\n<i>the new message is not in the list -> stays pending</i>
SESS -> CRD : append_history(session_id, [*new_context, bot answer])\n<i>does not contain the new message</i>
SESS -> CRD : clear_buffer(session_id)\n<i>DEL session:{id}:buffer - removes the whole key, new message included</i>
SESS -> CRD : clear_state(session_id)\n<i>DEL session:{id}:state -> IDLE</i>
note over CTRL, CRD
  the new message after the round ends
  PSQL: the row exists, status pending
  Redis: not in the buffer, not in the history, no chat job queued
  no line.reply for this message
  next chat round: the communicator does not see it (history comes from Redis)
  the new message is text: the analyser sees it (reads the whole session from PSQL - 4-6)
  the new message is an image: attachment.save never ran for it -> no file, no attachments row
    when the session is analysed, build_analyse_context raises ValidationError (4-6)
end note
@enduml
